[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mModule + login only (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mBuild the validation module and move login onto it. Signup gets built later against a proven interface. One real [39m
     [38;5;246mconsumer keeps the abstraction honest.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Module + login + signup
     [38;5;246mAlso add a signup form (email, password, confirm password) as a second consumer. Proves reuse for real, but expands
[39m     [38;5;246mscope into new UI and new markup decisions.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Module + login + a signup schema only
     [38;5;246mBuild the module, convert login, and define the signup rules in code without building its UI — so the rule set is [39m
     [38;5;246mready when the form is.[39m
